// REQUIRES: mpi
// A `for` over a distributed component that two archetypes hold: on many
// ranks, as partitions and as partitions one at a time in one process, it
// says what one process says, the lines it writes and the bits of the
// fractions it adds into a unique (Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent). The
// ranks wrote each rank's lines of both archetypes before the next rank's,
// and added each rank's rows of both before the next rank's; one
// partition at a time stopped where one gave the next a second fraction
// before it had taken the first. Fractions sent to cells of other ranks
// from both archetypes' rows were combined rank by rank, not archetype by
// archetype; and one partition at a time combined what was sent to its
// cells before the next had looked them up.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent --ranks 2 > %t.two
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent --ranks 3 > %t.three
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent --ranks 4 > %t.four
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.two
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.three
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.four
// RUN: %ent build %S/Inputs/ranks_two_archetypes.ent --ranks 4 --partitions -o %t.parts
// RUN: mpirun -n 1 -x ENT_RUNNING=1 %t.parts > %t.in1
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.in1
// RUN: mpirun -n 1 -x ENT_RUNNING=1 %t.parts > %t.in1b
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.in1b
// RUN: mpirun -n 2 --oversubscribe %t.parts > %t.in2
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.in2
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.four
// CHECK: 4 0.267403 13831355254831652229 3609 0
// CHECK: day 1: all 4796885293629908789 marked 4609149457883412100
// CHECK: 4 0.840459 13842578686594413665 10827 7290000
// CHECK: day 3: all 4806778231544703413 marked 4618003855687246251
